 Overview: 
 Our growing team is looking to fill the role of middleware administrator, specialized in administrating OpenShift. Please review the list of responsibilities and qualifications. While this is our ideal list, we will consider candidates that do not necessarily have all qualifications, but have experience, passion, and are ready to grow with us.
 If you’ll join our team, you will be challenged to: 
Support and document the installation, configuration, capacity planning, upgrading for all OpenShift environments;
Monitor and maintain optimal performance of OpenShift platform, execute performance tuning operations;
Ensure that OpenShift systems under administration are up to date in terms of security and updates;
Identifying, troubleshooting and resolving technical issues related to OpenShift in an incident. This may include identifying the root cause of the problem, finding a solution and implementing it;
Participate in intra and interdepartmental projects or activities, as requested by superiors or bank management, based on role and competencies, to contribute to the achievement of the bank's objectives.
 To perform in this role, we would like you to have: 
Very good hands-on experience in administrating OpenShift;
Very good knowledge of the Linux Operating system;
Analytical, problem solver, attention to details;
Teamwork, excellent communication and collaboration skills;
Relevant certifications may be an advantage.
 If you want to find out what other jobs we still have available, like Life at BT or what #Culture BT is, you can also access the Bank's career website : https://cariere.bancatransilvania.ro/
